 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 :claim
 {:level-1 {:statement "Codex closes APM problems."
            :status :established-and-uninteresting
            :note "A functioning of the machine. Not what this registers."}

  :level-2a {:statement "Memories extracted from solver closes, carried through
                         the memory medium, are USED by a weaker student on a
                         sound problem."
             :status :first-observed-at-F29
             :measures :functioning
             :note "F29 has attested student memory usage (Joe, 2026-08-24).
                    Usage is not yet improvement -- see level-2b."}

  :level-2b {:statement "The memories are LOAD-BEARING: the same student on the
                         same problem without them fails to solve."
             :status :not-yet-run
             :measures :functioning
             :design :tail-ablation
             :note "This is what turns 'used' into 'helped'. Requires student
                    rounds WITHOUT memory to demonstrate failure-to-solve."}

  :level-3 {:statement "A fully-stocked memory store lets the student close
                        HELD-OUT problems presumed beyond its independent
                        reach."
            :status :not-yet-attempted
            :measures :capability
            :note "Sen's distinction is load-bearing and is why this is a
                   SEPARATE claim, not a stronger version of level-2b.
                   Level-2b shows the student got better at what it could
                   already do -- a functioning. Level-3 shows the option set
                   itself expanded -- a capability. Only level-3 licenses the
                   downstream claim that the same medium could scaffold a
                   human (Joe's level #3)."}

  :level-3b
  {:statement "The SAME memory medium that lifts the machine student also lifts
               a HUMAN student -- i.e. the medium is substrate-neutral rather
               than machine-specific."
   :chain "Codex -> Zai/FUTON -> Joe. Level-3b is the FUTON -> Joe leg."
   :phase :separate
   :status :not-in-this-registration
   :measures :capability

   :phase-boundary
   "REGISTERED AS A SEPARATE PHASE (Joe, 2026-08-24). Level-3b is recorded here
    so that its prediction and its known confound are on the record BEFORE the
    phase-2 data lands, not because it is part of phase 2. Specifically:
    - it is NOT among the F29+ confirmation units;
    - it does NOT share the phase-2 ablation trigger or power band;
    - phase 2 is complete on its own terms whether or not 3b ever runs, and
      the absence of 3b is not a gap in this registration.
    Nothing in phase 2 is to be held open waiting for it."

   :why-not-just-a-repeat
   "3b is not level-2b performed on a human. It tests a property of the MEDIUM,
    not of a student. What transfers to the machine student is a mixture of
    conceptual moves and machine-specific API/tactic knowledge. If the same
    memories lift both, that is a strong claim about the medium and the
    delivery layer can be thin. If they lift the machine and not the human,
    the medium is machine-specific -- which is itself a real finding, and is
    the condition under which a genuine tutoring system (a TRANSLATION layer,
    not a delivery mechanism) becomes necessary."

   :sequencing
   "Do not build the tutoring system before phase 2 reports. The expensive
    question -- how much translation is needed -- is partly answered by the
    cheap experiment already running. Building first would spend the heavy
    lifting before knowing which kind of medium exists."

   :first-subject
   {:subject "Joe"
    :suitability
    "Methodologically apt as a rusty expert: prerequisites present, current
     fluency absent, which places him INSIDE the power band. A true novice
     would sit above it and reproduce the dead-with-deader comparison."
    :confound :not-blind
    :confound-detail
    "The first human subject designed the architecture, knows the hypothesis,
     and has read the memories. Any learning claim about him specifically is
     confounded past repair. Recorded NOW rather than discovered later."
    :consequence
    "Joe is the right subject for building and debugging the tutoring loop and
     the WRONG subject for any efficacy claim. An efficacy claim requires a
     different, blind learner."}

   :claim-scoping
   {:existence-proof
    "Senior knowledge mined, carried, and demonstrably used by a junior who
     could not do the task before. n may be 1. This is what the institutional-
     memory business case requires and is dramatically cheaper."
    :efficacy-trial
    "Learning gains across learners against a control. Required to make a
     PEDAGOGICAL claim. Not required for the business thesis, and not
     attempted in 3b."
    :rule "3b claims the existence proof ONLY. Any efficacy language in a 3b
           report is out of scope and should be refused."}}}

